<div class="reference-explainer">
  <div class="reference-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">FROM DISTANCE TO TARGET MOVEMENT</p>
    <h3>A defined target.<br/>An independent reference.</h3>
    <p>For movement observations against an independent reference, compare the distance to the same target at each observation. The reference stays independent of the movement being assessed; the measurement axis defines which component of movement is observed.</p>
    <div class="reference-formula"><strong>ΔD = D(t) − D₀</strong><span>Change in distance along the measuring axis</span></div>
    <p class="reference-acceptance">Specify the change your engineer needs to resolve, then verify target return, repeatability, temperature effects and reference stability at the site. A vertical settlement interpretation requires a vertical measuring arrangement or separately validated survey geometry.</p>
    <p class="reference-acceptance">For joint or bearing-gap observations, the mounting member is the relative reference. Absolute movement requires a separate stable survey reference.</p>
  </div>
